# Normalize line endings: store text as LF in the repo, let Git handle the
# working-copy conversion per platform. Silences the "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warnings and keeps diffs clean across Windows/Linux.
* text=auto

# Files that MUST stay LF even on Windows checkouts - they run on the Synology
# (Linux); CRLF would break the shebang / shell parsing.
*.sh   text eol=lf
# The app runs on the NAS too, and the JS tests cut functions out of
# dashboard.html by splitting on "\n" and looking for a bare "}" line - a CRLF
# checkout makes every line end in "\r" and those tests loop forever.
*.html text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Binary / data files Git should never touch line endings on.
*.db     binary
*.sqlite binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
